Q: Is there a way to save a flextable in R to a LaTex file? A: <p>I had the same issue multiple times when debugging flextable2pdf. Here are two options:</p>
<h2>1. With <code>rmarkdown::render</code> you can get a standalone <code>LaTeX</code>-file</h2>
<p>If you have a flextable inside a markdown file, you can render it to <code>LaTeX</code> using</p>
<pre><code>markdown &lt;- '
---
output:
  pdf_document:
  latex_engine: xelatex
---

```{r setup, include=FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(echo = FALSE)
suppressMessages(library(flextable))
```

```{r, echo=FALSE, warning=FALSE, message=FALSE, fig.width=9, fig.height=3, dpi=1200}
flextable(airquality[1:5, ])
```
'
temp &lt;- tempfile(fileext = &quot;.Rmd&quot;)
writeLines(markdown, temp)
rmarkdown::render(temp, output_format = &quot;latex_document&quot;, output_file = &quot;ft_standalone.tex&quot;, output_dir = getwd())
unlink(temp)
# tinytex::xelatex(&quot;ft_standalone.tex&quot;) # optionally generate PDF 
</code></pre>
